## Deploys and rollbacks

The pipeline deploys `main` to dev automatically and to production when someone starts the `deploy-production` job. Each deploy waits for the new pods to be ready and rolls back by itself if they aren't. To roll back a release that's ready but wrong, re-run the previous pipeline's deploy job, or revert the change and merge.

## Keeping up with the golden path

This service was generated from the platform's Python template. When the template improves, take the changes with:

```sh
copier update --trust
```

Review the result like any change; it arrives as a merge you can inspect, and your own edits are kept.
